# Golem

Instance `res://entities/player/player.tscn` in a level. Do not instance `res://addons/golem/player/player.tscn`.

`entities/player/player.tscn` is Lookey's player. It is based on the Golem player and already sets the body collision layer to 2 and the collision mask to 2049 (layer 1 `objects` and layer 12 `entity_collider`). The camera spring arm stays on layer 2. The mirror body and the real-world camera cull live in that scene, so every placed player gets them.

`addons/golem/player/player.tscn` is only a reference. Leave files under `vendor/golem` and `addons/golem` unchanged. From the game root, update that reference with `sh addons/golem/update.sh`.

Do not copy this repo's tests or its gdUnit4.

Name the node `Player` and attach `res://addons/golem/menu/golem_world.gd` only when the level should open the Escape menu.

The debug HUD stays in the player scene and starts hidden.

Action names, default keys, and the `toggle_mouse_mode` / `mouse_mode` split are in `addons/golem/docs/using-in-a-game.md`.
